{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem of painting two faces of a die blue such that the product of the numbers on the painted faces is not equal to 6, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of ways to paint two faces blue:**\n   A 6-sided die has 6 faces. The number of ways to choose 2 faces out of 6 is given by the combination formula \\(\\binom{6}{2}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\binom{6}{2} = \\frac{6!}{2!(6-2)!} = \\frac{6 \\times 5}{2 \\times 1} = 15\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the pairs of faces whose product is 6:**\n   We need to find pairs of numbers from 1 to 6 whose product is 6. The pairs are:\n   \\[\n   (1, 6), (2, 3), (3, 2), (6, 1)\n   \\]\n   Since we are choosing 2 faces, we only need to consider one of each pair (as the order does not matter). The valid pairs are:\n   \\[\n   (1, 6), (2, 3)\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":794,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,315,18824,1378,12300,315,264,2746,6303,1741,429,279,1985,315,279,5109,389,279,23983,12300,374,537,6144,311,220,21,11,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,2790,1372,315,5510,311,6177,1378,12300,6303,25,1019,256,362,220,21,49758,2746,702,220,21,12300,13,576,1372,315,5510,311,5157,220,17,12300,700,315,220,21,374,2661,553,279,10601,14806,1124,11520,6863,316,90,21,15170,17,11035,982,256,1124,9640,256,1124,6863,316,90,21,15170,17,92,284,1124,37018,90,21,0,15170,17,10297,21,12,17,41295,92,284,1124,37018,90,21,1124,15136,220,20,15170,17,1124,15136,220,16,92,284,220,16,20,198,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,28301,1437,279,13530,315,12300,6693,1985,374,220,21,25,1019,256,1205,1184,311,1477,13530,315,5109,504,220,16,311,220,21,6693,1985,374,220,21,13,576,13530,525,510,256,1124,9640,256,320,16,11,220,21,701,320,17,11,220,18,701,320,18,11,220,17,701,320,21,11,220,16,340,256,1124,921,256,8704,582,525,18774,220,17,12300,11,582,11